// The state schema: a component's state record, its named types, and its
// message buckets.
//
// Pure and target-agnostic like viewgen/ and cli/: source text in -> a typed
// StateDef out, never touching the filesystem. viewgen/ threads the result
// through view generation; cmd/main does the I/O.
//
// The surface used to be a subset of WIT, parsed with mizchi/wit. It is
// tutuca's own now, with a lexer and a parser in this package, and the reason
// is not taste: WIT cost a nesting level to say what a `<template id>` already
// says, two constructs for one idea because a C ABI needs the distinction,
// and — the one that showed everywhere — no per-declaration spans at all, so a
// semantic failure could only name an identifier and let the caller scan for
// it.
import {
  "moonbitlang/core/debug",
  "moonbitlang/core/json",
  "moonbitlang/core/string",
}
